[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Hide idle mouse pointer
Comment=checks/53: the KMS driver has no cursor plane, so a visible pointer is drawn in software, and X never page-flips while one is shown (full-screen games and video are then copied on the CPU). unclutter hides it after 1 s without movement.
Exec=unclutter --timeout 1
OnlyShowIn=XFCE;
X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=true
